    "longDescription": "iPerf3 TCP/UDP Client & Server brings the popular iperf3 network testing tool to Android — with a clean, Android-friendly UI.\n\nMeasure real throughput (bandwidth) between two endpoints and quickly spot bottlenecks in Wi-Fi, 5G/LTE, VPN, or Ethernet setups.\n\nImportant (so expectations are clear):\nThis is NOT a one-tap “ISP speed test”. iperf3 measures performance between a client and an iperf3 server. You’ll need either:\n• an existing iperf3 server on your network (router/NAS/server/PC), or\n• a second Android device running Server mode in this app.\n\nTypical use cases:\n• Verify Wi-Fi upgrades (new router/AP), channel changes, or AP placement\n• Compare Wi-Fi vs cellular vs VPN throughput\n• Troubleshoot slow LAN/WAN links and validate network changes\n• Check link quality in the field, lab, or data center\n• Measure UDP performance (jitter / packet loss) for real-time traffic scenarios\n\nWhat you can do:\n• Run iperf3 as a Client or as a Server (use your phone as the endpoint)\n• TCP and UDP throughput tests\n• Configure host, port, duration, parallel streams, reverse mode, and more\n• See detailed per-interval results and summaries after each run\n• Save results and logs for later reference\n• Works over Wi-Fi, cellular (4G/5G), VPN, and wired (Ethernet) connections\n• Simple, fast workflow — designed for engineers and power users\n\nQuick start:\n\n1. Start Server mode on one device (or use any reachable iperf3 server).\n2. Enter the server IP/host and port in Client mode.\n3. Choose TCP or UDP, adjust options if needed, and run the test.\n4. Review results and keep logs for troubleshooting and comparison.\n\nIf you need a lightweight “tap once and get Mbps” app, this probably isn’t it. But if you want accurate, repeatable iperf3 measurements and real diagnostics — this is built for that.",
